    "result_text": "The only test source is the acceptance suite, and it's green (2/2 passing, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the rule that creating an owner whose normalized telephone collides with an existing owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/DuplicateTelephoneException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signalling the collision, mirroring the existing `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `addOwner` now normalizes the telephone (as before), then calls a new `requireUniqueTelephone(...)` guard before saving. The guard compares the incoming normalized number against every existing owner's telephone, normalized the same way (non-digits stripped), so the check holds regardless of how stored numbers were originally formatted. On a match it throws `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateTelephoneException` returning `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail` whose `errors` array reports `telephone`, consistent with the other owner-validation handlers.\n\nThe check runs after normalization and after the existing required-field/telephone-format validation, so a distinct telephone still yields a 2xx create (verified by `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and a duplicate yields 409 (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`).",
